{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Potentially Successful Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications",
  "Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1621\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Potentially Successful Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications\" or \"<ip>|Potentially Successful Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications\"\n\nSame conditions as 'Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications' (5+ pushes, or 3+ pushes with 2+ denied/unanswered/abandoned prompts, per user in the search window), followed by at least one successful MFA in the same window: the user may have approved an attacker's prompt. Risk floor Critical (90).\n\nFalse positives: a user who fumbled several prompts and then approved their own. Confirm with the user.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_potentially_successful_okta_bombing_via_push_notifications/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_potentially_successful_okta_bombing_via_push_notifications.toml",
  "GUID": "6438b4a1-ccd5-56b3-8583-ff8a37be74f1",
